# Plan Completion Gate

Part of the always-on set in **`agent-discipline-core.mdc`** (pre-close checklist item 1–2). Applies to **every non-trivial code change**—bugfixes, hotfixes, refactors, and plan-driven work—not only when the user asks to **implement a plan**. Treat the **close sequence** as a deliverable, not optional prose after tests pass.

**Hard gate:** **Do not mark the task, plan, or any todo done** until:

1. **Final code review** (senior-engineer pass on the diff and affected workflows) finds no unfixed gaps,
2. **Structured chat self-review** (step 2 below) is written in the **same final turn**, and
3. **When implementing a plan:** plan YAML todos synced (`status: completed` for every finished step; see **Plan YAML todo sync** below) and the **`post-implementation-review`** todo is complete.

See **`plan-template-enforcement.mdc`** for request phrasing and PLAN_TEMPLATE alignment.

## Blocking close gate (required chat headings)

Before any final message that reports work **done**, **fixed**, **ready**, or **complete**, the agent **must** include these sections **in order**:

1. **`## Agent rule dispatch`** — Pre-close checklist **#5** in **`agent-discipline-core.mdc`**: list every triggered **`hpcperfstats/cursor-rules/*.mdc`** file you **Read** (tool) **before the first edit** in the turn, or **`N/A`** only when edited paths did not trigger domain rules. The Cursor **`stop`** hook auto-detects triggered rules from edited paths (via **`hook_task_router.py`**), rejects invalid **`N/A`**, requires dispatch listing, verifies **Read** tool calls (always-on rules exempt), and requires **≥3** edge-case bullets.
2. **`## Final code review (senior engineer pass)`** — Senior Software Engineer review of the **full diff** and **every workflow touched**; checklist-style findings; **fix gaps before close**.
3. **`## Post-implementation review`** with subsections **`### Why it works`**, **`### Edge cases`** (≥3 realistic failure modes), **`### Convention check`**.

**Forbidden without all sections above:** marking todos completed; phrases like “done”, “complete”, “ready to ship”, “fix is in tree”, “task is finished”.

**User enforcement:** if the user replies **`Close gate incomplete`**, redo the full close sequence without argument.

**Cursor hook:** project `stop` hook `.cursor/hooks/check-close-gate.py` auto-submits the same follow-up when a code-changing turn ends without required headings (`loop_limit: 3`). See `.cursor/hooks/README.md`.

**Narrow exceptions:** answer-only questions with no code; trivial typo/comment-only edits with no behavioral contract.

## Plan YAML todo sync (during implementation)

The **plan file frontmatter** (for example `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`) is what the **Plan UI** shows. Session `TodoWrite` alone does **not** update that UI.

**When implementing a plan:**

1. **Canonical ids** — read todo `id` values from the plan YAML at task start; use those **exact** ids in `TodoWrite` (do not invent aliases like `rules-docs-minimal` when the plan says `rules-docs-sync`).
2. **On each step complete** — when work for a plan todo is done, set that todo’s `status: completed` in the plan frontmatter **in the same turn** (status-only edit).
3. **“Do not edit the plan”** — when the user forbids plan edits, that means **do not change plan prose, scope, or approach**; **status-only** frontmatter updates remain **required** unless the user explicitly forbids all plan file writes.
4. **Before task close** — verify no plan todo remains `status: pending` except items the user explicitly deferred; if any are still pending, either finish them or state the deferral in chat—do not claim the plan is complete.

Committed design docs under **`docs/plans/`** marked read-only by the user: same status-only rule applies only when that file is the active implementation checklist; otherwise sync the Cursor Plan file attached to the task.

## Close sequence (mandatory order)

Same content as **Blocking close gate** above, expanded. Run all steps in the **same final turn** that reports implementation done, **before** marking todos complete.

### 0. Agent rule dispatch

Per **`agent-discipline-core.mdc`** task router: for each triggered domain rule, confirm you **Read** it before editing. In chat, under **`## Agent rule dispatch`**, list basenames (for example `sync-timedb-archive-janitor-contract.mdc`) or state **`N/A`** when the diff touched no router trigger paths. The Cursor **`stop`** hook rejects an empty dispatch section and emits **`Rule not read: <name>`** when a listed domain rule has no **Read** tool call on that `.mdc` in the transcript for this turn.

### 1. Final code review (senior engineer pass)

Act as a **Senior Software Engineer**. Review the **full diff** and every **workflow the change touches**—callers, tests, compose runners, config and docs sync, cross-layer wiring—not only the files edited.

Look for:

- correctness and behavior regressions
- performance regressions
- missing components (tests, docs, registry or drift guards, API client or tools updates, nginx or route sync when applicable)
- edge cases not covered by tests
- anything else a senior reviewer would block on merge

**Fix anything found** and re-run relevant tests. Do not proceed to step 2 or mark todos complete while open review items remain.

Aligns with **`plan-creation-contract.mdc`** step 6 and **`docs/plans/PLAN_TEMPLATE.md`** → *Final code review*.

### 2. Structured chat self-review

After the senior pass is clean, write these three headings in chat (per **`implementation-review-workflow.mdc`**):

1. **Why it works** — one short paragraph tying the diff to the plan and upstream contracts (API, ingest, config, cache, tests).
2. **Edge cases** — at least **three** realistic failure modes still possible (concurrency, stale state, partial ingest, auth, missing fixtures, operator misconfig).
3. **Convention check** — naming, imports, test placement, docs/`test_runs/` logging, every **triggered** workspace rule (cite rule names when non-obvious), and confirmation that the senior review pass found no unfixed gaps.

If writing the chat sections surfaces a new gap, return to step 1, fix, re-test, then update the chat sections.

## Plan todos (mandatory last item)

Every implementation plan YAML must include a final todo:

```yaml
- id: post-implementation-review
  content: "Final senior code review (diff + workflow) clean; structured self-review in chat (why it works, edge cases, convention check)"
  status: pending
```

Do not mark this todo **completed** until **both** close-sequence steps above are done (or a narrow exception below applies).

## Runtime logic changes

When behavior changes, also run **`logic-change-checklist.mdc`** mentally and confirm in **Convention check**: invariants, failure modes, regression tests, and compose/host test tier match the change.

## Test and artifact bar

- Executed tests reported with pass/fail; blockers documented per **`test-first-discipline.mdc`**.
- Run artifacts under **`test_runs/`**, not **`docs/`**, per **`test-runs-output-directory.mdc`**.
- Plan frontmatter: all implementation todos `status: completed` (or explicit deferral documented) before reporting done.

## Narrow exceptions

- Answer-only questions with no code.
- Trivial typo/comment-only edits with no behavioral contract.

